2026-09-27T09:27:25.9988499Z Description:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9988867Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9989168Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9989868Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9990735Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9990831Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9991052Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9991339Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9991596Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9991693Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9991901Z ================
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9992031Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9992187Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9992726Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9992936Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9993044Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9993537Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9993694Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9993831Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9994221Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9994567Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9995187Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9995663Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9995766Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9996179Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9996688Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9996949Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9997237Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9997602Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9997695Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9997887Z ========
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0070106Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0071535Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0073092Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0073371Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0073854Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0074739Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0075309Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0075828Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0076249Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0076654Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0076760Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0077044Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0077181Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0078160Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0079202Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0079801Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0080599Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:27:26.0080809Z 
